Nothing in this skill searches your source for secret-shaped strings. No author
name or address, no commit message, no branch or tag name and no file path is
emitted. Every value above was checked against a declared allowlist before it was
written. Two disclosed exceptions sit beside that, both described in
references/client-runbook.md section 4: the content digest reads every file's
bytes, and a --build authentication failure checks the checkout's own registry
configuration. Neither retains anything it read.

